    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1170">

                <pb facs="1011" n="907" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg907"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/63.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d1170-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-12-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 15, 1913</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>This morning the Spanish Minister at this capital called to ask me to have the
                    various authorities at El Paso, Texas, thanked for their kindness to Spanish
                    refugees at that place.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson O’Shaughnessy</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1170-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1170-f1-content">
                <p>Transmitted by the Department December 16 to the Red Cross and the Mayor of El
                    Paso.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
